outcome.summary:
Round 2, tree 5d87ef33c. Round-1 findings are fixed except one new case that still fails on some dates.

Verified OK:
- wait_task_waiting() is gone. waits_with_reason() requires exactly WAITING with '-', unplanned_with_reason() exactly UNPLANNED with the exact reason. The prefix match is used only for the two UNREACHABLE checks with varying numbers.
- MAX_PLAN_ITEMS = MAX_PLAN_RUNS (indigo_agent_scheduler.c:66) is safe. Plan items come only from plan_runs[0..runs). The planners store hook runs in the same array and stop at max_runs (init_state, simulate, store_final_hooks, vis_store in indigo_agent_scheduler_plan.c). The update_plan loop (3133) is also bounded.
- The chosen hours hold across the year, with margins of hours. At the equator the day length stays within about 7 min of 12 h and the equation of time within about 16 min, so the plan lasts 18 h +/- 0.5 h at H=12 (until the sunrise after the next sunset) and 10 h +/- 0.5 h at H=20 (until sunrise). The scheduler night only extends the end when night->end is after sunrise, which it is not with the default night offsets. Margins:
  - South needs about 11.3 h;
  - Steep, Low and Thin air under 1.2 h;
  - Long look about 13.5 h;
  - Night only runs after dusk;
  - East needs 20.9 h against 18 h (UNPLANNED), Low sides 2 h and then 4 h (WAITING);
  - Outside and Gap open in 1-2 h against 10 h; the next window of Too short is 23.5 h away;
  - TooShort and the cases without a site do not depend on the clock;
  - Later opens within 1 h against 10 h.
- No other remaining task-list assertion depends on the wall-clock hour. sky_bonuses (fixed 17.11) asserts only the start order. wait_task_reachable in the unreachable case accepts QUEUED or a plan reason, which is a correct reachable outcome either way.

Defect:
- indigo_test/integration/test_agent_scheduler.c:3142 (moon_separation_and_brightness) requires Fixed to be UNPLANNED 'too close to the moon'. The site has the moon at the zenith, so its local time follows the moo

