Defect:
- indigo_test/integration/test_agent_scheduler.c:3142 (moon_separation_and_brightness) requires Fixed to be UNPLANNED 'too close to the moon'. The site has the moon at the zenith, so its local time follows the moon phase, and the plan can last up to about 23 h. Over that time the moon moves up to about 12-15 degrees in RA and about 6 degrees in declination. Fixed's limit, ceil(separation + 8) at line 3131, leaves only 8 degrees of margin. So on the next day's pass the separation can exceed the limit while the target is above 20 degrees, Fixed gets a run and stays WAITING.
  - Evidence: I simulated the case geometry with the scheduler's own sky code (indigo_scheduler_sky_build, target/points build, points_next up to indigo_scheduler_night_end, MIN_ALTITUDE 20) hourly over 2027-2028, 16825 samples with the moon high. Fixed was planned in 235 of them (1.4%), for example moon declination 2.7 degrees, 9 days from full, separation 12, limit 20, run at +21.6 h with the plan ending at +22.6 h.
  - Beside (3 degrees against a 30-degree limit), Never and Lorentzian never failed. With ceil(separation + 16) or + 20, Fixed failed 0 times.
  - Fix: widen Fixed's margin (+16 is enough in the simulation), or assert Fixed only as never started with the REASON instead of UNPLANNED.

Test runs: make -C indigo_test test-agent-scheduler gave 199 of 200. visibility_due_run_starts_after_a_run failed ('Starting task Target' timeout at 3448). This case is not changed by the ticket and the same intermittent failure is already recorded in archived ticket 1dc2b4a0, so it is a pre-existing flake. The round-1 tree gave 200 of 200.
